🔴 p.put3 / p.same3 / p.close3 / p.trap3: zerobas prints NOTHING where the
   CF-3300 answers OK. ~~the THIRD PUT of a session hangs, untrappably~~ --
   WITHDRAWN (D-PUT3SLOW 2026-09-02): nothing hangs, every row completes at a
   longer step. And D-PUTCOST (2026-09-06) then measured the work on the
   guest's own TIME clock: 1.71 ticks/PUT here against 2.14 on the CF-3300,
   and this exact three-PUT program runs in 6 ticks = 0.12 s. So it is not
   slow EITHER, and what makes these rows blank at step=2.5 is UNKNOWN.
   p.put1/p.put2/p.trap2 are the controls.

🔴 ALL OF THE ABOVE IS SUPERSEDED (D-CLOSEFLUSH, 2026-09-06). Run with
   ZEROBAS_REFCACHE=0, p.put3 / p.same3 / p.trap3 / k.put3 / x.l1p3 /
   x.l0p3 all read OK on zb: EVERY three-PUT row WITHOUT a close passes.
   The rows that still fail -- p.close3, ctl.128.*, s.100.*, s.96.r6 --
   are exactly the ones that CLOSE and reopen after a write. Measured by
   bisecting the harness completion budget: 3 writes + GET is 0.05s on
   both machines; 1 write + CLOSE + reopen + GET is 3.51s on the CF-3300
   and >24s here; a CLOSE with NO write is 0.05s on both.
   ⚠️ AND THAT PARAGRAPH IS ITSELF RETRACTED (D-PUTFLOOR, same day). It
   rested on two instrument bugs: a run_gap below `step` is a NO-OP (the
   harness takes max(t_run+step, t_run+run_gap)), and the per-case .dsk
   path was keyed on the LINE COUNT so different programs shared one
   mounted image the emulator writes to. With both fixed, cache off and
   three repeats: 3 writes + GET and NO close reads <NO OUTPUT> on zb
   while 1 write + GET reads BBB. The WRITE COUNT is the subject; the
   close is separately expensive on BOTH machines and is its own question.
   ⚠️ The zb ctl.128.* rows below are BLIND FOR THAT REASON (they write three
   records), so they are NOT evidence about record layout.

